comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-14T05:49:24.833Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete2959-item all-status corpus plus Sentry trace search and fresh open/in-progress reads; closed pm-58yzil delivers explicit consent tracing and remains completed. New operational acceptance scope: fresh CLI trace and spans queries return empty, spans API metadata ingestion.status=stalled. Project-scoped stats in04:00-06:00UTC show3 accepted transactions and3 accepted/indexed spans, plus24 client-discard spans reason no_parent_span; this aggregate does not identify the traced action. No root-cause claim or fabricated errors. Private receipts retained locally; no credentials or installation identity recorded."
  "2026-10-14T05:51:42.141Z","harness:codex","Additional fresh hosted logs and explicit-project spans queries also report ingestion.status=stalled and return no rows. Project-scoped outcomes prove accepted diagnostic traffic, but accepted-volume totals are not action-specific trace freshness. Keep this operational acceptance task open; no global tracing policy, sampling default or Sentry project settings were changed."
  "2026-10-14T16:20:41.387Z","harness:codex","Fresh2026-10-14T16:18UTC verification after current work: sentry issue list is:unresolved returns no rows; strict Sentry/telemetry gate passes with max-critical0/max-high0 and required telemetry, finish_error_rate_pct3.18 and failures_without_error_code_rows0. Explicit fresh1h trace query still returns no rows. Telemetry physical flush separately drained1 queued row to0 with queue_empty=true and last_successful_flush_at16:18:06Z. These are separate claims: no action-specific hosted trace freshness proven, so existing operational acceptance remains open/unclaimed. No Sentry policy or global sampling setting was changed."
  "2026-10-14T17:21:53.786Z","harness:codex","Latest explicit successful audited comments mutation used PM_SENTRY_TRACE_COMMANDS=1 and SENTRY_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE=1 without changing persisted consent or global sampling. The command and telemetry drain complete normally, but a subsequent fresh1h trace query still returns0 rows. This does not prove an ingestion root cause or a current action-specific hosted trace; retain the existing open operational acceptance and distinguish it from healthy queue delivery,70/70 finite-cohort pairing and the passing threshold gate."
  "2026-10-14T17:38:32.925Z","harness:codex","Fresh-trace diagnostic 2026-10-14T17:37Z: explicit PM_SENTRY_TRACE_COMMANDS=1 and SENTRY_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE=1 permit tracing and initialize the Sentry SDK in the current build (both booleans true). This distinguishes local consent/init from hosted visibility; it does not establish ingestion or explain the earlier empty fresh-trace queries. The threshold gate and finite telemetry pairing remain separate evidence. No global consent/policy changed and no synthetic error was sent."
  "2026-10-14T18:14:57.657Z","harness:codex","18:14UTC observability refresh: fresh1h hosted trace list still returns0 rows with hasMore=false. Native telemetry flush at18:12:15Z reports queue_empty=true,0 entries, no failed flush; private installation-scoped fixed16:05-18:11UTC cohort has145 starts/145 finishes,0 unmatched/duplicate sessions, and3 separate error-only sessions. All6 Prometheus targets report up=1. These current delivery and pairing facts do not establish action-specific Sentry trace freshness or its root cause. Retain this operational acceptance as open/unclaimed; no consent, sampling or project policy was changed."
  "2026-10-14T18:59:15.887Z","harness:codex","Real necessary CLI stats action at18:51:44UTC used explicit tracing and100% per-process sampling through the supported embedded CLI. A passive Node HTTP diagnostic observer recorded Sentry response200; the actual Sentry client was initialized and its bounded flush completed=true. No request body, headers, DSN, trace identity or credential was retained. A subsequent fresh1h trace query still has0 rows/hasMore=false. Current client transport acceptance is therefore proven separately from hosted trace visibility. Next acceptance: correlate the accepted action window with project span ingestion/indexing outcomes and a privacy-safe queryable trace; preserve consent/free-tier policy and do not manufacture errors. This task remains open/unclaimed."
  "2026-10-14T19:09:12.972Z","harness:codex","Exact-correlation acceptance now verified: capture the real successful supported embedded CLI stats command span through a passive beforeEnvelope observer, preserving explicit configured consent and per-process sampling. The captured identity matches a fresh hosted trace view returning1 root span, pm stats, op pm.command, start2026-10-14T19:05:43.693Z and duration3181ms; HTTP200 and bounded flush=true were independently observed. No raw argv values, credentials or private trace identity are recorded here. Generic trace listing still returns0, and the CLI warns that individual span details could not be fetched. Those discovery/detail limitations do not negate the directly queryable current root span; earlier empty-list/stalled metadata was not proof of absent ingestion. This fulfills the existing current-trace acceptance without changing consent, sampling defaults, project settings or free-tier policy."
  "2026-10-14T20:26:07.956Z","harness:codex","Fresh final-source operational proof: a real successful pm stats command started2026-10-14T20:12:51.571Z, exported one root pm.command span with HTTP200 and successful flush, and matched the exact span in a fresh hosted Sentry trace query. Observed duration663ms. No trace/span/installation identifiers retained in this public evidence; consent/sampling opt-in was per-process and persistent configuration unchanged. Span-detail enrichment still reports its fetch warning, separately from successful root-trace retrieval."
  "2026-10-14T22:04:31.489Z","harness:codex","Final frozen source SDK and embedded CLI probe: successful real pm stats at 2026-10-14T22:01:30.808Z was matched to its exact hosted root span through a fresh project-qualified Sentry trace query; op pm.command, duration 746ms, flush true. The project-qualified trace view returns one matching root span; detail enrichment still warns it could not fetch span details. This is real successful command evidence after the final privacy and declaration changes, with no synthetic external error and no consent policy change. All six telemetry stack targets are up in the separate current check."
  "2026-10-24T12:33:42.459Z","harness:codex","October24 bounded recheck on the completed trace-verification owner: the project-qualified fresh Sentry trace list returns a complete empty result for24h and1h. A single successful contracts summary read was explicitly traced with existing telemetry consent, PM_SENTRY_TRACE_COMMANDS=1 and sample rate1; the subsequent fresh1h query still returned no rows after several minutes. Earlier delivered successful-trace evidence remains historical and this does not reopen that completed scope. Current trace freshness is unverified, separately from the passing issue gate, paired production telemetry and queue checks. Preserve this observation for the next focused diagnostics without inventing a hosted span or forcing persistent consent."
  "2026-10-24T12:37:25.707Z","harness:codex","Correction/expanded discovery evidence: project-qualified sentry span list --fresh --period1h now returns a current pm contracts row after the explicitly traced probe, while generic trace list remains empty. This is span-ingestion evidence rather than a missing-ingestion defect; do not infer absence from the trace-list surface. Timestamp/op and trace-detail projection are being checked separately. No runtime or persistent-consent change is required by this SDK continuation delivery."
  "2026-10-24T12:39:08.192Z","harness:codex","Fresh span ingestion is confirmed from the unprojected span-list result: successful pm contracts, op pm.command, start2026-10-24T12:21:53Z. The CLI normalizes fields to op/start_timestamp/duration_ms/project_slug, so requesting advertised timestamp/span.op/trace fields had hidden those coordinates. Generic trace list remains empty and this span-list row has no trace identity; do not claim trace-detail or symbolication evidence. The current successful-command span is real hosted data, with no synthetic error or persistent sampling/consent change."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-14T19:09:13.985Z","harness:codex","For streamed Sentry spans, correlate a real action to its exported trace identity and query that exact trace. Empty generic listings and per-span detail warnings are separate discovery results, not proof that the action was never ingested. Record safe command identity, timestamps and transport acknowledgement while keeping private trace identities out of public PM evidence."
close_reason: Verified a current successful command trace by exact identity in hosted Sentry
